course: dictionary
lesson: 15743
title: Traverse: crossing a place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Traverse is a formal word for travelling across or through a place. «The explorers traversed the desert» means they crossed the desert from one side to the other. Everyday speech would just say «crossed», so traverse is a more formal way to say it.
explain: Context helps you here. «The explorers traversed the desert over twelve days» tells you it was a long journey across sand. Swap in crossed and the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Traverse can also mean going back and forth over something. «The guard traversed the castle wall, checking every tower.» In climbing, a traverse is a route that goes sideways across a slope or cliff, not straight up. Look at the clues in the sentence to tell which meaning is used.
fact: Traverse means to travel across or through a place.
fact: «The explorers traversed the desert» means they crossed the desert.
fact: Traverse is a formal word; in everyday speech people usually say cross.
fact: In climbing, a traverse is a route that goes sideways across a slope or cliff.
fact: In maths, traversing a shape or network means going along every edge of it.
exercise: «The explorers traversed the desert in twelve days.» What does traversed mean? | *Crossed | Rested in | Dug holes in | Ran away from
exercise: Mia says traverse means to dig a hole. What is the right meaning? | To sleep in a tent | To dig under the ground | *To travel across or through a place | To fly high in the sky
exercise: «The climbers made a traverse across the cliff face, not a climb straight up.» What is a traverse here? | A short, slippery rest stop | *A route that goes sideways across a slope or cliff | A tall, straight climb to the top | A rope tied to a tree
test: «The guard traversed the castle wall, checking every tower.» What does traversed suggest? | Fell off the wall | Built a new tower | *Went along and across the wall | Painted the wall
test: Grandad says a walk over the moor traverses the hills. Which word could you swap in? | Sleeps | Forgets | Paints | *Crosses
exam: A pupil traverses every edge of a cube without lifting the pen. What does traverses mean here? | Draws a circle around it | Makes the cube bigger | Counts only the corners | *Goes along every edge
